.page hostname 1 print or set the name of this machine

# SYNOPSIS
*hostname* [_NAME_]

# DESCRIPTION
`hostname` prints the host name, the first line of `/Hakurei/etc/hostname`; it is `gensokyo` out of the box, and also when the file is missing or does not hold a name. uname(1), the shell prompt and the `HOSTNAME` variable show the same name.

With _NAME_, root renames the machine: the name goes into `/Hakurei/etc/hostname` and, when a HUMANVILLAGE volume is mounted, is kept there so it is still the name after a restart (see etckeep(8)). A name is made of letters, digits and `-`, does not start or end with `-`, and has at most 31 characters. New shells and programs see it at once.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for a bad name, a file that cannot be written, or a caller who is not root; 2 for a usage error.

# EXAMPLES
    hostname
    sudo hostname hakugyokurou

# SEE ALSO
uname(1), etckeep(8)
